> telelport / dig me down a  level), if I see another cat in  the 
> dungeon is there a way for me to make a pet out  of it?  Is it 
> even worth it, or should I seriously consider doing it? 

Early on pets are very useful* [in fact I generally use several 
until I reach minetown, which is usually after I do Sokoban, 
unless I'm having food supply problems]. Untame cats and dogs 
(slightly less so when the moon is full) will eat most types of 
food, and there's no better way of making such a pet than feeding 
it [use the smallst food item you can - save their favourite for 
rewards...]. Horses I tend to avoid as pets (unless I'm going to 
be riding one), they're a bit too finicky about heir food. If I 
lose a housecat, I try and replace it with a housecat (or bigger). 


There are ways of getting other monsters as pets, either by being 
extra charming, using a scroll of taming, or a wand/potion/trap of 
polymorph on an existing pet. 

*some people don't like playing with pets, though, if you decide 
they're not worth the effort abandon them, or set an option in 
your settings file to not have pets.

